%% A single chat turn: from reader's "send" click to the doc updating.
%% Shows the WebSocket message types and the snapshot / validator path.

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Reader
  participant Viewer
  participant WS as WebSocket
  participant Runtime as Agent runtime
  participant SDK as Claude SDK
  participant FS as docs/[slug]/

  Reader->>Viewer: types prompt + clicks Send
  Viewer->>WS: {type:"chat", text, context:{doc, selections}}
  WS->>Runtime: run_turn(prompt)

  Note over Runtime,SDK: Inline doc into preamble<br/>so agent skips a Read

  Runtime->>SDK: query(prompt + doc context)

  loop For each tool call
    SDK->>Runtime: pre_tool_use_hook(Edit)
    Runtime->>FS: save_snapshot(before_text)
    Runtime-->>SDK: allow

    SDK->>FS: write current.md
    FS-->>SDK: ok

    SDK->>Runtime: post_tool_use_hook
    Runtime->>Runtime: validators.validate_doc(new_text)

    alt Validation passes
      Runtime->>FS: detect_id_drift + record pending
      Runtime->>WS: broadcast({type:"doc_changed"})
      WS->>Viewer: doc_changed
      Viewer->>FS: GET current.md
      FS-->>Viewer: latest text
      Viewer->>Viewer: re-render doc
    else Validation fails
      Runtime->>FS: revert from snapshot
      Runtime-->>SDK: additionalContext: error<br/>(agent retries)
    end
  end

  SDK-->>Runtime: turn_done (cost_usd)
  Runtime->>WS: broadcast(turn_done)
  WS->>Viewer: turn_done
  Viewer->>Reader: spinner stops
